eight=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> P, Q, R, S</p>\n<p>When object is at infinity, a real, inverted and diminished image is formed at F. When the object is brought closer to the lens. The image moves away from the lens and increase in size. (Image is between F and 2F). when the object is at 2F', the image is formed at 2F. The image is real, inverted and is of the same size. When the object is moved closer between 2F' and F', the image is real, inverted and magnified. When the object is at F' the image is real, inverted, highly magnified and is formed at infinity.</p>\n<p>(D) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> P, Q, R, S</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgnd6qwk/a3bba25a-5a81-4155-90f8-ad7b05daa210/ad461740-de82-11ed-b183-b94b9634bbd5/file-1lgnd6qwl.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lgnd6qwk/a3bba25a-5a81-4155-90f8-ad7b05daa210/ad461740-de82-11ed-b183-b94b9634bbd5/file-1lgnd6qwl.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 23 English Explanation\" srcset=\"ht